pt09 adversarial lane, surface: risk-flag detectors. Greens the RED frozen in
the previous commit.

`STATISTIC_SHAPES` replaces the inline pattern and adds the two forms the
detector could not see: a word-form percentage in either register
("80 per cent", "80 percent") and a ratio spelled out ("more than one in
five"). The strip inside the guard grows with the detector, for the reason it
existed — a bare quantity must not count as its own evidence that the quantity
is sourced.

The regex is `g` and therefore stateful, so both reads go through
`statisticShapes()`, which resets `lastIndex` first. Without that, `.test()`
answers differently on the same string depending on what was asked of it
before, and the test pins that two reads agree.

Corpus census that motivated it: 665 symbol-form percentages, 127 word-form,
14 spelled ratios. About one statistic in six in the archive was spelled in a
way the detector could not see, and the British-register sources are almost
entirely word form. `chooseDestination`, one function away in the same file,
already routed on the word.

Cost, measured — and this is the first fix in this run that moves anything:

- 6 research-queue items across 2 sources gain `unsupported statistic`
  (04-heteropessimism x1, 15-asc-american-friendship x5). No item loses a
  flag, and no destination changes.
- 0 of 1,299 corpus stance rows move; no score moves; no label moves.
  `classifyRiskFlags` runs only for unmapped residue and reaches nothing that
  scores, so there is no threshold crossing to rule.
- Gate floors identical: 191 · 1.0000 · 1.0000 · 0.8529.

All 18 suite steps green.

